<title>JAPAN: Taiyo Yuden defies weak market trend.</title>
<headline>Taiyo Yuden defies weak market trend.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese electrical machinery maker Taiyo Yuden Co Ltd was up in Friday afternoon trade, as investors were impressed by the issue's ability to buck the recent weak trend in the stock market, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0451 GMT, the shares were up 40 yen at 1,620 yen, exceeding the previous high for the year by 10 yen.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors were encouraged by the share price which was unscathed by falls in the Nikkei average,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said. &quot;The issue renewed its high for the year today which should make investors appreciate it even more.&quot;</p>
</text>
